<title>UK: Cointel to raise $400 mln in bonds this week.</title>
<headline>Cointel to raise $400 mln in bonds this week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's Compania de Inversiones en Telecomunicaciones SA (Cointel) plans to raise $400 million in international debt this week, bankers said on Monday.</p>
<p>Cointel will issue a $200 million seven-year bond and a 200 million Argentine peso ($200 million) seven-year bond as well, London bankers said.</p>
<p>Goldman Sachs and Merrill Lynch were tipped as joint lead managers for the transaction.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748 ($ = 0.999 Argentine Pesos)</p>
